A||N||4||Xtreme Fiero's||what does the ECM control?||||4||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||12-09-2000||10:03 AM||||<BR>Since my deal on an awsome 85 GT fell through I have been thinking about rebuilding my parts car, The car is fine from the doors up, I will just need a deck lid I facia to look like a fiero again. I have a 5-speed for it but in needs a motor. so If I used a carbed 2.8-3.2Lcould I get rid of the ECM & engine harness (already gone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ). I know I will need new gauges (don't have them any way) Is there any thing else the ECM controls?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-09-2000||10:17 AM||||speedo and fuel pump are the only things I can think of.<BR>ways around the fuel pump, not sure about the speedo.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PlasticWrapd||12-09-2000||01:41 PM||||You can always leave the ECM in the car and disconnect the stuff that you aren't using.  Remove the "check engine" bulb too so it doesn't stay on all the time.  <P>One thing you might consider...  Maryland has a yearly emissions test (except on the Eastern Shore).  You may be able to meet the actual emissions standards with a carbed engine, but it WILL NOT pass the visual inspection.  The Fiero never had a carbed version in the USA (or anywhere else as far as I know).  The minute they open the engine compartment, the car will fail.<p>[This message has been edited by PlasticWrapd (edited 12-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||12-09-2000||01:46 PM||||of the three car I have had on the road two ov them have had visual inspections (they looked for a cat with a mirror) I have never seen them lift the hood on any car even when i was waiting in line. mabye it depends on the county.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||12-09-2000||03:02 PM||||Don't forget that the ECM advances the spark timing.  If you do away with the ECM, the carbed engine you put in should have a distributor with centrifugal and vacuum advance... or replace the ECM-controlled distributor with a centrifugal+vacuum one.  This assumes you want it to run well (as opposed to, "well, run."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).<P>If you would like such a distributor, I've an old HEI distributor (from a non-Fiero 2.8)I'd be willing to sell you one cheap.  But all the fiddling around to make it work well is up to you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>To answer your original question, the ECM controls fuel pump, fuel injection, ignition timing, EGR, idle speed, A/C compressor engagement, and perhaps a few other items I'm not thinking of at the moment.  Some of those functions can be bypassed or "worked" with nonelectronic controls fairly easily.  Others could be fairly difficult        ||||reg||4
